course: dictionary
lesson: 10084
title: Words for helpers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A therapist is a trained person who helps people get better from an illness, an injury or a problem. Many therapists help without medicine or an operation, often by talking and by practising skills.
explain: Read the context to work out which kind of therapist is meant. «A stammer is when words get stuck or repeat when speaking; letting the person finish is the kind thing to do, and speech therapists can help.» Stuck words are about speaking, so the helper is a speech therapist.
explain: A word that comes before therapist, like speech, physio or play, tells you what the therapist helps with. Use that clue to guess the job, then check a dictionary if you are not sure.
fact: A therapist is a trained person who helps people get better from illness, injury or problems.
fact: Many therapists help without drugs or surgery.
fact: Some therapists help with feelings and thoughts by talking, like a counsellor.
fact: «Speech therapist» means a therapist who helps people with talking and sounds.
fact: Seeing a therapist is normal and brave, just like going to a doctor.
exercise: «A stammer is when words get stuck or repeat when speaking; letting the person finish is the kind thing to do, and speech therapists can help.» Which therapist helps with stuck words? | Dentist | *Speech therapist | Physiotherapist | Chef
exercise: What does a therapist do? | Drives buses to school | *Helps people get better from illness, injury or problems | Sells tickets at the cinema | Makes food in a restaurant
exercise: Priya hurt her arm in a fall and needs exercises to move it again. Which therapist might help her? | Play therapist | Speech therapist | Occupational therapist for handwriting | *Physiotherapist
test: Which therapist helps with handwriting and everyday skills? | Speech therapist | Play therapist | Physiotherapist | *Occupational therapist
test: Which therapist can help a child with big worries and feelings? | Physiotherapist | *Play therapist | Speech therapist for sounds | Dentist
exam: Which statement about therapists is true? | Therapists only work in schools | *Seeing a therapist is normal and brave | Only adults can see a therapist | Therapists never talk to people
